\pard\sa0\sl276\slmult1\li0 WHAT'S NEXT\par
\pard\sa0\sl276\slmult1\li0 ------------------------------------------------------------------\par
\pard\sa0\sl276\slmult1\li0 - THE REMINDERS \u8212? FINISHED (#12-new). Nothing left to build. All\par
\pard\sa0\sl276\slmult1\li240 eight steps are in, and one piece of the app now owns every\par
\pard\sa0\sl276\slmult1\li240 reminder on the phone. The plan that ran this work is no longer\par
\pard\sa0\sl276\slmult1\li240 a live file; it is kept whole at the end of docs/build-history.md\par
\pard\sa0\sl276\slmult1\li240 in case anyone ever needs to know why a thing was done its way.\par
\pard\sa0\sl276\slmult1\li240 What was built, step by step:\par
\pard\sa0\sl276\slmult1\li480 Step 1 (#6-new) \u8212? the new piece itself, plus its tests. No\par
\pard\sa0\sl276\slmult1\li720 page touched.\par
\pard\sa0\sl276\slmult1\li480 Step 2 (#7-new) \u8212? My Day and Pets stopped arming their own.\par
\pard\sa0\sl276\slmult1\li720 This is the fix for the silence.\par
\pard\sa0\sl276\slmult1\li480 Step 3 (#8-new) \u8212? My Week, Look Ahead and To-Do stopped too,\par
\pard\sa0\sl276\slmult1\li720 and Orders came out of the reminding altogether.\par
\pard\sa0\sl276\slmult1\li480 Step 4 \u8212? the snoozes, delays and postpones, in three pieces:\par
\pard\sa0\sl276\slmult1\li720 My Week's postpone and Look Ahead's delay (#9-new), then My\par
\pard\sa0\sl276\slmult1\li720 Day's and Pets' snoozes (#10-new), and then To-Do (#11-new),\par
\pard\sa0\sl276\slmult1\li720 which needed nothing built. A To-Do banner has never had a\par
\pard\sa0\sl276\slmult1\li720 Snooze button to tap, so the piece was taking out code that\par
\pard\sa0\sl276\slmult1\li720 could never run.\par
\pard\sa0\sl276\slmult1\li480 Step 5 (#11-new) \u8212? the Memory Test's five-minute recall.\par
\pard\sa0\sl276\slmult1\li480 Step 6 (#11-new) \u8212? the warning when your phone can't hold\par
\pard\sa0\sl276\slmult1\li720 every reminder asked for. It shows as you save the item,\par
\pard\sa0\sl276\slmult1\li720 on the page you're on, and says the reminder furthest in\par
\pard\sa0\sl276\slmult1\li720 the future won't go off until something makes room.\par
\pard\sa0\sl276\slmult1\li480 Step 7 (#11-new) \u8212? the clean slate. Yesterday's checkmarks,\par
\pard\sa0\sl276\slmult1\li720 snoozes and counts now clear whether or not you open My Day\par
\pard\sa0\sl276\slmult1\li720 or Pets, and any banner from before today is taken down as\par
\pard\sa0\sl276\slmult1\li720 the app opens or comes back to the front. A Done always\par
\pard\sa0\sl276\slmult1\li720 means today now.\par
\pard\sa0\sl276\slmult1\li480 Step 8 (#12-new) \u8212? Scheduled Reminders, in Settings under the\par
\pard\sa0\sl276\slmult1\li720 three reminder times. It shows every reminder your phone is\par
\pard\sa0\sl276\slmult1\li720 holding, under Today, Tomorrow, This Week and Later, with\par
\pard\sa0\sl276\slmult1\li720 the soonest first. Tap any one and you get the whole story\par
\pard\sa0\sl276\slmult1\li720 of it: what it is, which page it came from, when it fires\par
\pard\sa0\sl276\slmult1\li720 and whether it repeats, when it was last due and when it's\par
\pard\sa0\sl276\slmult1\li720 next due, exactly what the banner will say, and which\par
\pard\sa0\sl276\slmult1\li720 buttons it will carry. At the foot it tells you how full\par
\pard\sa0\sl276\slmult1\li720 the phone is. Timer alerts are counted there but not\par
\pard\sa0\sl276\slmult1\li720 listed, your call \u8212? the Timer is for short stretches and\par
\pard\sa0\sl276\slmult1\li720 isn't something you'd look up.\par
\pard\sa0\sl276\slmult1\li720 It cannot tell you whether a reminder actually went off.\par
\pard\sa0\sl276\slmult1\li720 The phone keeps no record of that once a banner is\par
\pard\sa0\sl276\slmult1\li720 dismissed, so there is nothing to read. What it does\par
\pard\sa0\sl276\slmult1\li720 instead is show you when each one was DUE \u8212? so if a\par
\pard\sa0\sl276\slmult1\li720 repeating reminder is missing from the list, that's the\par
\pard\sa0\sl276\slmult1\li720 problem; if it's sitting there properly set and you heard\par
\pard\sa0\sl276\slmult1\li720 nothing, the app did its part.\par
\pard\sa0\sl276\slmult1\li240 You built all of this, put it on the phone, and it was all\par
\pard\sa0\sl276\slmult1\li240 readable. What still hasn't happened is the morning after.\par
\pard\sa0\sl276\slmult1\li0 - The clock setter is off by twelve hours (#5-new). Spinning the\par
\pard\sa0\sl276\slmult1\li240 hour down from the 12:00 PM it opens at goes to 11 PM instead\par
\pard\sa0\sl276\slmult1\li240 of 11 AM, so setting 9 in the morning the natural way lands on\par
\pard\sa0\sl276\slmult1\li240 9 at night \u8212? which is your evening banner. Typing the time is\par
\pard\sa0\sl276\slmult1\li240 fine, and so is the AM/PM button. Small fix on its own. After\par
\pard\sa0\sl276\slmult1\li240 it, any time you set by spinning needs checking.\par
\pard\sa0\sl276\slmult1\li0 - Look Ahead: change the tile format, and change or drop the\par
\pard\sa0\sl276\slmult1\li240 Snooze (#3-new).\par
\pard\sa0\sl276\slmult1\li0 - Timer: add a Stop (Pause) / Continue (Go) button to the tile,\par
\pard\sa0\sl276\slmult1\li240 and add a log (#3-new).\par
\pard\sa0\sl276\slmult1\li0 - Vault restructuring: the "Home" header button becomes a "Back"\par
\pard\sa0\sl276\slmult1\li240 button (#3-new).\par
